              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"> 
                <b><font size="3">PMWATCH - April 18 2002</font></b><font size="3"> 
                -- As yesterday's and today's papers illustrate, the US media 
                is beginning to move away from the Jenin story, as though everything 
                that needs to be known about what took place there last week has 
                now been conclusively established. The fact is that, no official, 
                independent investigation has been conducted, journalists have 
                not been given free access to the whole camp, and the IDF is still 
                shooting its tanks within Jenin.</font></font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">And 
                yet, otherwise respectable journalists, such as the Washington 
                Post's Molly Moore, have concluded that "no evidence has 
                surfaced to support allegations by Palestinian groups and aid 
                organizations of large-scale massacres or executions by Israeli 
                troops" (see story below). The story was written two days 
                ago -- April 16 -- barely hours after the IDF escorted a few journalists 
                into some specific areas in the camp, for brief period of time.</font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">Contrast 
                this to the headline from Phil Reeves, April 18, 2002: "Fresh 
                evidence of Jenin atrocities" (see below).</font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">Contrast 
                this also to Amnesty International's call "on the UN Security 
                Council to order an urgent investigation into alleged abuses at 
                the West Bank refugee camp of Jenin" (See below).</font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">Please 
                impress the media to cover this important story professionally.</font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">More 
                importantly, impress upon them the need to take statements from 
                credible human rights group more seriously than statements from 
                the IDF. (See: <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/unmission.asp">http://www.pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/unmission.asp 
                ) </a></font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">Fill 
                in the interface below and click send. Your letter will be sent 
                to the emails below. </font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">Please 
                also consider calling your paper. To find phone numbers of your 
                foreign desk editor or ombudsman, please go to: <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/volunteer/calling.html">http://www.pmwatch.org/pmw/volunteer/calling.html</a></font></p>
